    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d136-a1-a1">

                <pb facs="0331" n="311" xml:id="pg311"/>

                <head>Earl Russell to Mr.
                        Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Foreign Office,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-09-12"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 12, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your letter of the 6th instant, respecting the case of the Alabama and the
                    proceedings, on the occasion of the sinking of that vessel, of the owner of the
                    Deerhound; and I have to inform you that your communication will receive a reply
                    as soon as it can be prepared.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with the highest consideration, sir, your most obedient,
                    humble servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>RUSSELL.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
